native32: the x87 ring, inline runtime helpers, O(1) import names and per-site call caching on MSVC

- recomp_types.h: RECOMP_X87_RING builds with MSVC (RECOMP_X87_UNLIKELY instead of
  __builtin_expect); RECOMP_X87_RING_DEPTH keeps g_fp_top counting pushes minus pops;
  RECOMP_X87_ST/PUSH/POP reach the lifted x87 stack from runtime and host code under either
  model; RECOMP_HELPER force-inlines the per-instruction flag and x87 helpers (recomp_cond,
  recomp_cond_cf, recomp_carry, recomp_flags_pack, recomp_parity8, the ring, fp_round_cw,
  fp_st0_to_i64); fp_round_cw gives the C library's results without its calls;
  RECOMP_ICALL_SITE_RANGE gives each indirect call site a two-entry cache of the targets inside
  [g_recomp_site_lo, g_recomp_site_hi) and the shim page, without GCC statement expressions.
- native32.c: the ring's storage and recomp_x87_recentre, thread state saved from and loaded
  to the ring, float returns of native calls and callbacks through the accessors, an
  open-addressing table for native32_name, the cacheable ranges and native32_is_shim.
- x87crt.c, native32_selftest.c: the accessors instead of g_st.

Applied by tools/fetch_pcrecomp.py on top of the commit in config/target.json (series order).

